# rc.d scripts and shell scripts must keep LF endings. FreeBSD's sh rejects a
# CRLF file mid-statement with a message that points at the wrong line, and
# Git Bash tolerates it, so the fault only appears on the target platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this directory, so `rc.d/*` would
# only ever have matched a top-level rc.d. The scripts live in hajime-*/rc.d.
**/rc.d/* text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf

# The generated art. Marked binary so a diff shows "changed" rather than a
# thousand lines of mangled bytes, and so the eol=lf rule above never touches
# them: a PNG with its 0x0d bytes rewritten is a PNG that no longer decodes.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.ico binary
# The console art and the loader's Lua carry real escape bytes and tabs. They
# are text, and they must reach FreeBSD with LF endings like every other script.
*.ansi text eol=lf
*.lua text eol=lf
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify
